window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b3f105b8b2d4ada0"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"review-budget-vs-actuals\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">复核预算与实际</h1> <p>将计划、实际数据和结账说明整理成差异分析工作簿。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供预算、实际数据导出文件和结账说明，请它将实际数据对应到预算计划、计算差异、标出对账问题，并区分有依据的解释和仍待回答的财务问题。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>在月末将预算计划与实际支出导出数据进行比较的复核。</li> <li>根据总账、支出或部门实际数据，为管理层准备说明的财务团队。</li> <li>需要复核类别映射、勾稽结果和缺乏依据的解释的工作簿。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>检查表格输入、清理并映射行数据、创建差异表，并生成可供复核的工作簿。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>复核预算与实际</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $spreadsheets，根据随附文件更新预算与实际复核表。\n\n将实际数据与计划进行比较，把实际数据映射到正确的预算类别，总结主要差异，并制作一份可编辑的 .xlsx 工作簿，便于复核。\n\n保留原始输入；用公式计算金额差异和百分比差异；对于无法明确映射的类别，请标记出来，不要强行匹配。根据科目类型判断差异是有利还是不利：收入高于计划属于有利差异，费用高于计划属于不利差异。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent 技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">简介</h2> <p>如果你正在处理预算，并希望复核差异或检查问题，ChatGPT 可以帮助你创建一份可实际使用的复核工作簿。</p> <p>附上预算计划、实际数据导出文件和结账说明，然后请 ChatGPT 生成一份可编辑的复核工作簿。它可以保留原始输入、将实际数据映射到预算计划、计算差异，并创建可在聊天中检查的摘要视图。</p> <p><a id=\"create-the-review-workbook\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">创建复核工作簿</h2> <ol> <li>附上预算计划、实际数据导出文件和结账说明；或者提供准确的文件引用及其来源。</li> <li>使用起始提示词，并要求生成可编辑的 <code>.xlsx</code> 工作簿。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT 中打开工作簿，并展开到全屏，检查原始输入、数据映射、差异公式和摘要工作表。</li> <li>继续在同一聊天中修正类别映射、添加部门切分，或起草财务总结。</li> </ol> <p>如果来源文件位于已连接的插件中，请明确指出要用的文件或文件夹。如果复核必须基于指定的财务资料，就不要让 ChatGPT 搜索整个 Drive 或整个工作区。工作簿出现在聊天中后，先打开并全屏检查原始输入、映射、差异公式和摘要工作表，再要求修改。</p> <p><a id=\"check-the-variances\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">检查差异</h2> <p>分享工作簿之前，请 ChatGPT 审查类别、公式和差异说明。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check the budget vs. actuals review before I share it.\n\nList:\n\n- the most material unfavorable variances by dollar impact\n- the most material favorable variances by dollar impact\n- categories that may be mapped incorrectly\n- accounts where the favorable or unfavorable sign convention is unclear\n- explanations supported by the close notes\n- explanations that need human review\n- formula or tie-out issues in the workbook\n\nFix safe formatting or formula issues, then list anything finance should resolve before leadership review.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请在我分享之前，检查这份预算与实际情况对比分析。\n\n列出：\n\n- 按美元影响衡量，最重大的不利差异\n- 按美元影响衡量，最重大的有利差异\n- 可能存在映射错误的类别\n- 有利或不利差异的正负号约定不明确的科目\n- 有结账说明支持的解释\n- 需要人工审阅的解释\n- 工作簿中的公式或勾稽核对问题\n\n修复可以安全处理的格式或公式问题，然后列出财务部门在提交领导层审阅之前应解决的事项。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"review-budget-vs-actuals\">Review budget vs. actuals</h1> <p>Turn plan, actuals, and close notes into a variance workbook.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT a budget, actuals export, and close notes, then ask it to map actuals to plan, calculate variances, flag reconciliation issues, and separate supported explanations from open finance questions.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Month-end reviews that compare budget plans with actual spend exports.</li> <li>Finance teams preparing leadership commentary from GL, spend, or department actuals.</li> <li>Workbooks where category mapping, tie-outs, and unsupported explanations need review.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Inspect spreadsheet inputs, clean and map rows, create variance tables, and produce reviewable workbook outputs.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Review budget vs. actuals</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $spreadsheets to update the budget vs. actuals review from the attached files.\n\nCompare actuals to plan, map actuals to the right budget categories, summarize the major variances, and prepare a clean review view as an editable .xlsx workbook.\n\nPreserve the raw inputs, use formulas for dollar and percentage variance calculations, and flag categories that do not map cleanly instead of forcing a match. Use account type to determine favorable or unfavorable variance: revenue above plan is favorable, while expense above plan is unfavorable.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>If you're working on a budget and want to review the variances or inspect any issues, ChatGPT can help you create a fully functional review workbook you can work with.</p> <p>Attach the budget plan, actuals export, and close notes, then ask ChatGPT for an editable review workbook. ChatGPT can preserve the raw inputs, map actuals to plan, calculate variances, and create a summary view you can inspect in the chat.</p> <h2 id=\"create-the-review-workbook\">Create the review workbook</h2> <ol> <li>Attach the budget plan, actuals export, and close notes, or provide exact file references along with the source.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and ask for an editable <code>.xlsx</code> workbook.</li> <li>Open the workbook in ChatGPT. Expand it into the full-screen view to inspect the raw inputs, mappings, variance formulas, and summary tab.</li> <li>Continue in the same chat to fix category mappings, add department cuts, or draft the finance summary.</li> </ol> <p>If the source files are in a connected plugin, mention the exact files or folder. Avoid asking ChatGPT to search a broad Drive or workspace when the review should use specific finance sources. When the workbook appears in the chat, open it and expand it full-screen to review the raw inputs, mappings, variance formulas, and summary tab before asking for revisions.</p> <h2 id=\"check-the-variances\">Check the variances</h2> <p>Before sharing the workbook, ask ChatGPT to audit the categories, formulas, and variance explanations.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Check the budget vs. actuals review before I share it.\n\nList:\n\n- the most material unfavorable variances by dollar impact\n- the most material favorable variances by dollar impact\n- categories that may be mapped incorrectly\n- accounts where the favorable or unfavorable sign convention is unclear\n- explanations supported by the close notes\n- explanations that need human review\n- formula or tie-out issues in the workbook\n\nFix safe formatting or formula issues, then list anything finance should resolve before leadership review.\n</code></pre>"};
